     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Il giorno giovedì 18 febbraio 2021 alle 15:17:16 UTC <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dca...@iastate.edu</a> ha scritto:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Paolo, \r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">The code you sent seems to simply be the linear model table output.  However, I believe your question gets at whether one should interpret the separate versus\r\n common allometry analyses and plots. Part of that is evaluating the linear model table and making a determination as to the importance of the interaction term; as you did in your email. Then, once one makes that determination, the plot from the corresponding\r\n model is used. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Below is an example of this, adjusted from the help file for plotAllometry.  First I fit a linear model that includes the slope test (i.e., the interaction),\r\n and then the common allometry analysis and plot.  One could use this, plus biological judgement, as a guide.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><br>\r\nBest, <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><br>\r\nDean<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">##<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">data(plethodon)\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Y.gpa &lt;- gpagen(plethodon$land, print.progress = FALSE)    #GPA-alignment \r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">gps &lt;- interaction(plethodon$site, plethodon$species)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">gdf &lt;- geomorph.data.frame(Y.gpa, gps  = gps)\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"># Group Allometries<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">fit &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ Csize * gps, data=gdf, iter=999,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">                print.progress = FALSE)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">#NOTE INTERACTION DOES NOT PROVIDE EVIDENCE OF HETEROGENEOUS SLOPES<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">anova(fit)  \r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"># Predline: Plotting anyway for illustration<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">plotAllometry(fit, size = gdf$Csize, logsz = TRUE, method = &quot;PredLine&quot;,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">              pch = 19, col = gps)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"># Common Allometry<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"># Group Allometries<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">fit.c &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ Csize + gps, data=gdf, iter=999,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">                print.progress = FALSE)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">anova(fit.c)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"># Predline<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">plotAllometry(fit.c, size = gdf$Csize, logsz = TRUE, method = &quot;PredLine&quot;,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">              pch = 19, col = gps)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dr. Dean C. Adams<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Director of Graduate Education, EEB Program<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Professor<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Iowa State University<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><a href=\"https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484172563000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3pC7KYmZqordQIBjPJhr7n\">https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">515-294-3834</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div><div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b><a rel=\"nofollow\">moccett...@gmail.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Thursday, February 18, 2021 4:44 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] unique allometry<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">Hi everyone,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">I’m analysing data from 4 different users that have landmarked the same specimens.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">Apparently, different users (&quot;Obs&quot; in the code) follow different allometry patterns, although the amount of variation explained by unique allometry is just 2.5 %. That shouldn’t be possible as the specimens landmarked by different\r\n users are exactly the same. I guess this is simply caused by variations in where users are putting landmarks.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">The predline plot shows a single regression line.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">How would you interpret this? I think I would simply assume a common allometry model. Would this be correct?</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">See attached code and plot.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">Many thanks</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\">Paolo</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div></div><div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/ec225a17-7e75-4029-86d9-880f421526e1n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/ec225a17-7e75-4029-86d9-880f421526e1n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484172563000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2mmbim2_pqxVIObH6VQ3mQ\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/ec225a17-7e75-4029-86d9-880f421526e1n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div>"
